const faqs = [
  { q: "What is Gift Crafting?", a: "A feature released on February 8, 2026, that lets you combine up to 4 collectible gifts into one new, unique gift at Uncommon, Rare, Epic, or Legendary rarity. Each tier gets its own artwork and visual effects." },
  { q: "How much does crafting cost in Stars?", a: "Crafting itself doesn't charge a separate Stars fee — the \"cost\" is the collectible gifts you feed into it. If the result later needs to be formalized as an on-chain NFT, that can require a separate upgrade payment." },
  { q: "How do you improve the success chance?", a: "Two ways: (1) adding more gifts (up to 4) and using higher-rarity ones both raise the odds; (2) using gifts that share attributes increases the chance those attributes carry over into the crafted result." },
  { q: "What happens if a craft fails?", a: "Every gift you put in is destroyed completely — there's no refund or partial compensation. Telegram describes this openly as a risk-based mechanic, so only feed in gifts you can afford to lose." },
  { q: "Are Gift Crafting and Gift Upgrade the same thing?", a: "No, they're completely different mechanics. Upgrade converts one ordinary gift into a collectible (NFT) for a Stars fee. Crafting combines several gifts that are already collectibles into one new, rarer gift." },
  { q: "Can you sell a crafted Legendary gift?", a: "Yes — the result is a full collectible gift, sellable on Telegram's Gift Marketplace or through Fragment. Higher-rarity crafted gifts typically command significantly higher prices." }
];
