  <section>
    <p class="post-lead"><strong>Short answer:</strong> on February 8, 2026, Telegram launched <strong>Gift Crafting</strong> — combine up to 4 collectible gifts into a new one at <strong>Uncommon, Rare, Epic, or Legendary</strong> rarity. More gifts, and higher-rarity ones, raise your odds of success — but on failure, <strong>every gift you put in is destroyed</strong>. This is a completely different mechanic from upgrade, which turns an ordinary gift into a collectible.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What is Gift Crafting?</h2>
    <p>Gift Crafting shipped alongside Telegram's biggest-ever Android redesign: the ability to combine several gifts that are already collectibles (converted to NFTs) into a single new gift at a higher rarity tier. The result is a unique item with its own artwork and visual effects.</p>
    <p>If you're not sure what a collectible gift actually is, the concept is covered in Telegram's own gift documentation — a regular gift becomes a collectible through the separate "upgrade" process, which pays a Stars fee to mint it on-chain.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How it works, step by step</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Open the Gifts section</strong> — you need at least 2 collectible gifts.</li>
      <li><strong>Switch to Crafting mode</strong> — find the crafting section in your gift list.</li>
      <li><strong>Pick 2-4 gifts</strong> — the more you add, the better your odds.</li>
      <li><strong>Check the success odds</strong> — the system shows a success percentage and the possible resulting rarity.</li>
      <li><strong>Confirm</strong> — success gets you a new gift; failure destroys everything you put in.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What determines the success chance?</h2>
    <p>Two main factors. First, <strong>quantity and rarity</strong>: adding more gifts (up to a maximum of 4) and using higher-rarity ones both raise your odds. Second, <strong>matching attributes</strong>: feeding in gifts that share the same Model, Backdrop, or Symbol increases the chance those specific attributes carry over into the final crafted gift. So the outcome isn't purely random — which gifts you choose partially shapes the result.</p>
  </section>

