          <tr><td>Cost</td><td>Stars (on-chain fee)</td><td>The gifts you feed in</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Result</td><td>A collectible (NFT) version of that same gift</td><td>A brand-new, higher-rarity gift</td></tr>
          <tr class="highlight-row"><td>Failure risk</td><td>None — always produces a collectible</td><td>Real — all input gifts can be lost</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Can you sell a crafted gift?</h2>
    <p>Yes — the result is a full collectible gift, sellable on Telegram's Gift Marketplace or through Fragment. Higher-rarity gifts tend to sell for significantly more: see <a href="/en/blog/most-expensive-telegram-gifts">the most expensive Telegram gifts</a> for record sale prices. For how the selling process works, read <a href="/en/blog/sell-telegram-gift-fragment">how to sell a Telegram gift on Fragment</a>.</p>
  </section>

